From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: ricktav <82380971+ricktav@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 24 Nov 2026 08:45:59 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] ASoC: apple: s8000-mca: Leave the interrupt alone on every A7
 MCA

The iPad Air's MCA0 (apple,s5l8960x-mca) storms like the iPad mini 2's
MCA1 did before apple,s5l8960x-mca-tdm got no_irq: on a J71 the line
stays asserted at boot with both version 1 enables clear and no known
cause in the status register, 100000 unhandled interrupts, then "irq 62:
nobody cared" and "Disabling IRQ #62". Playback keeps working after
that, as it is DMA-driven.

Set no_irq on the I2S variant too, so no A7 MCA requests its interrupt.
Nothing on the J71/J72 path depends on it: the handler only acks and
masks error causes (with a rate-limited debug message); it reports no
underrun or fault to ALSA.

Signed-off-by: ricktav <82380971+ricktav@users.noreply.github.com>
Assisted-by: LLM
Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 sound/soc/apple/s8000-mca.c | 13 ++++++++-----
 1 file changed, 8 insertions(+), 5 deletions(-)

diff --git a/sound/soc/apple/s8000-mca.c b/sound/soc/apple/s8000-mca.c
index 00270d00de79a..184b1038c36da 100644
--- a/sound/soc/apple/s8000-mca.c
+++ b/sound/soc/apple/s8000-mca.c
@@ -268,11 +268,13 @@ struct s8000_mca_hw {
 	unsigned int sync_bits;		/* 0: half a frame */
 	u32 stream_irqs;		/* error causes open while TX is prepared */
 	/*
-	 * Leave the interrupt line alone. On the iPad mini 2 (J85), A7 MCA1's
-	 * line stayed asserted with both version 1 enables clear and no known
-	 * cause in the status register: 100000 unhandled interrupts during
-	 * the first prepare, which starved the touchscreen's SPI firmware
-	 * upload.
+	 * Leave the interrupt line alone. On the A7 the line stays asserted
+	 * with both version 1 enables clear and no known cause in the status
+	 * register, on MCA0 (iPad Air, J71) as on MCA1 (iPad mini 2, J85):
+	 * 100000 unhandled interrupts, then "nobody cared". On the J85 that
+	 * starved the touchscreen's SPI firmware upload. Playback is
+	 * DMA-driven and the handler only masks error causes, so nothing
+	 * else depends on it.
 	 */
 	bool no_irq;
 	/*
@@ -1484,6 +1486,7 @@ static const struct s8000_mca_hw t7001_mca_hw = {
  */
 static const struct s8000_mca_hw s5l8960x_mca_hw = {
 	.version = 1,
+	.no_irq = true,
 	.regs = &mca_v1_regs,
 	.dai_format = SND_SOC_DAIFMT_I2S,
 	.v1_ctl = MCA_V1_XX_CTL_A7,
